\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Symmetric ZCA whitening and quorum voting on two correlated dials ($\sigma _1{=}1.9$, $\sigma _2{=}1.0$, $\rho {=}0.88$). (a)\nobreakspace  {}On raw errors, a coordinated shift hides inside the naive 1D box and inflated scalar circle, while a hijacker false-alarms. (b)\nobreakspace  {}ZCA yields unit-variance ($\sigma $) axes; dashed lines mark dynamic $98.5$th-percentile tripwires $\pm \tau _j$. Pink corners require $2/2$ dials, whereas the $128$-dial model sets count quorum $K_{\text  {Lite}}$ dynamically per stream.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
